# .dockerignore - files Docker leaves out when it builds the image (the "build context").
#
# The Dockerfile copies the project into the image (COPY . .), and in Phase 5 that image is pushed
# to AWS. So anything personal or secret must be listed here, or it would end up inside the image:
# - .env: API keys are passed in at run time (docker-compose.yml locally, Secrets Manager on AWS).
# - my_docs/, evals/private/, evals/audio/: your real CV, job posts, emails, the eval cases built
#   from your real answers, and your recordings. Personal data: never in an image.
# - evals/*/runs/: local eval summaries.
# - .git, .venv, __pycache__, .pytest_cache: history and local caches the app does not need.
# - infra: Terraform files (Phase 5), used from your machine or CI only.
# - logo/: design files, not used by the app.
# When you add a folder with personal data, add it here and to .gitignore.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
my_docs
evals/private
evals/audio
evals/*/runs
.git
.venv
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
infra
logo
brief_edit.json
